<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43202" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτερο-ρρεπής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, 
			Act.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>making now one side
				and now another preponderate</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					403
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>inclining to one side or the other</i>, of patients in the
			crisis of a disease, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i><i>Acut.(Sp.</i>)<i><span class="en">
				21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one-sided</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. ζήτημα</span>
			where the <i>weight</i> of evidence <i>preponderates</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Stat.</u>
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῶς</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				8.13
			</span></i>.</div>
